@startuml push-consumer-close
title v5 PushConsumer close() — Full Shutdown Sequence

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam participantPadding 15
skinparam boxPadding 8

actor "Application" as App

box "v5 Client SDK" #LightBlue
    participant "PushConsumer\n.close()" as PC
    participant "PushConsumerImpl\n.shutDown()" as PCI
    participant "ProcessQueue\n(per queue)" as PQ
    participant "ConsumptionExecutor\n(ThreadPool)" as Exec
    participant "MessageListener\n(user code)" as ML
    participant "ClientImpl\n.shutDown()" as CI
end box

box "Proxy" #LightYellow
    participant "ReceiptHandle\nProcessor" as RHP
end box

box "Broker" #LightGreen
    participant "AckMessage\nProcessor" as AMP
    participant "PopRevive\nService" as Revive
end box

== Step 0: Application calls close() ==

App -> PC : close()
PC -> PCI : stopAsync().awaitTerminated()\n[Guava Service lifecycle]

== Step 1: Stop new assignments (no new ProcessQueues) ==

PCI -> PCI : scanAssignmentsFuture.cancel(false)
note right
  Stops periodic queue assignment scan.
  No new MessageQueue assigned.
  No new ProcessQueue created.
  Existing ProcessQueues continue receiving.
end note

== Step 2: Wait for inflight receive requests ==

PCI -> PCI : waitingReceiveRequestFinished()
note right
  maxWait = requestTimeout + longPollingTimeout
           = 3s + 30s = 33s (default)
  Poll inflightReceiveRequestCount every 100ms.
  Waits until 0 or timeout.
  Ensures all POP responses received and
  messages cached in ProcessQueue.
end note

loop until inflightReceiveRequestCount == 0 OR timeout
    PCI -> PCI : sleep(100ms)\ncheck inflightReceiveRequestCount
end

== Step 3: Shutdown consumptionExecutor ==

PCI -> Exec : shutdown()\n+ awaitTerminated()
note right
  Waits for all running MessageListener
  callbacks to finish.
  No new consume tasks accepted after shutdown().
end note

loop for each running consume task
    Exec -> ML : [already running] consume(messageView, ctx)
    ML --> Exec : ConsumeResult.SUCCESS / FAILURE
    Exec -> PQ : eraseMessage(mv, result)
    alt SUCCESS
        PQ -> AMP : AckMessageRequest (async)
        AMP --> PQ : AckResult.OK
    else FAILURE
        PQ -> RHP : ChangeInvisibleDurationRequest\n(retryPolicy.getNextAttemptDelay)
        RHP --> PQ : new receiptHandle
    end
end

== Step 4: 1s grace for async ACK/NACK RPCs ==

PCI -> PCI : sleep(1s)
note right
  Best-effort window for async ACK/NACK
  RPCs (submitted during step 3) to complete.
  Not guaranteed — fire-and-forget.
end note

== Step 5: super.shutDown() — ClientImpl ==

PCI -> CI : super.shutDown()

CI -> CI : notifyClientTermination()\n→ gRPC NOTIFY_CLIENT_TERMINATION to proxy
CI -> CI : updateRouteCacheFuture.cancel(false)
CI -> CI : telemetryCommandExecutor.shutdown()\n+ awaitTerminated()
CI -> CI : releaseClientSessions()\n→ close all gRPC telemetry streams
CI -> CI : clientManager.stopAsync().awaitTerminated()\n→ close all gRPC channels
CI -> CI : clientCallbackExecutor.shutdown()
CI --> PCI : done

PCI --> PC : shutDown() complete
PC --> App : close() returns

== What happens to unfinished messages ==

note over PQ, Revive
  Messages NOT acked before channel closes:
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Cached but never dispatched to listener                      │
  │   → CK natural expiry → PopReviveService → %RETRY%group     │
  │                                                              │
  │ Listener was running, didn't finish before executor shutdown │
  │   → No ACK/NACK sent → CK natural expiry → revive           │
  │                                                              │
  │ ACK/NACK RPC not completed within 1s sleep                  │
  │   → Channel closed → proxy detects CLIENT_UNREGISTER         │
  │   → CLEAR_GROUP → changeInvisibleTime(1s)                   │
  │   → ~1s later → revive → %RETRY%group                       │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
end note

RHP -> RHP : CLIENT_UNREGISTER event\n→ clearGroup(channel, group)\n→ changeInvisibleTime(1s) for all handles
note right of RHP
  Fastest re-delivery path:
  ~1s after channel close,
  message visible to other consumers.
end note

RHP -> Revive : [~1s] CK expires
Revive -> Revive : reviveRetry()\n→ %RETRY%group\n(reconsumeTimes+1)

@enduml
